  "visible_text": "BIOLOGICAL SYSTEMS / CONTROL DESK 04\n\nCell Gatekeeper\n\nGate the membrane. Place the required selective leak, watch a passive crossing, and eject it. Then place and fuel the sodium and potassium ATP pumps until both concentration pairs enter their target bands. Keep every bar inside its target band for 6 transport ticks, then lock. Use only screenshots and visible task controls in this webpage; do not use code, scripts, Developer Tools, console, debugger, inspector, network, source, DOM or page-state inspection, terminal, shell, Python, address-bar or URL edits, reload/navigation, extensions, external applications, hidden state, or unrelated tabs.\n\nFULL INPUT\nLIVE CLOCK\nt+051\n01 / TARGET LOCK\nREADY TO LOCK\n\nEvery concentration pair must sit inside its amber band for the visible hold window. A pump consumes ATP; a leak keeps diffusing until it is ejected.\n\nNa+ pump\nPlace it and fuel it with ATP until the sodium bars enter the target bands.\nK+ pump\nPlace it and fuel it with ATP until the potassium bars enter the target bands.\nNa+ leak\nPlace it, watch one passive crossing, then eject it before the final lock.\n02 / MEMBRANE WINDOW\nCROSSING DETECTED\nOUTSIDE\nextracellular\nINSIDE\ncytoplasm\n1NA+ PUMP\n2K+ PUMP\n3EMPTY\n4EMPTY\nDROP SOLUTE\nOUTSIDE\nDROP SOLUTE\nINSIDE\nTRANSPORT TRACE\nK+ pump \u00b7 ATP outside \u2192 inside\n03 / CONCENTRATION BARS\nCAPACITY 30\nNa+\nOUT 10\u201312 \u00b7 IN 7\u20139\nOUT\n12\nIN\n7\nK+\nOUT 9\u201311 \u00b7 IN 9\u201311\nOUT\n10\nIN\n10\n04 / PROTEIN DRAWER\nDRAG TO SLOT\n\u2194\nNa+ selective leak\nPASSIVE \u00b7 high concentration \u2192 low concentration\n\u21c4\nK+ ATP pump\nACTIVE \u00b7 outside \u2192 inside \u00b7 ATP required\n\u2194\nK+ selective leak\nPASSIVE \u00b7 high concentration \u2192 low concentration\n\u21c4\nNa+ ATP pump\nACTIVE \u00b7 inside \u2192 outside \u00b7 ATP required\nDRAG A MEMBRANE PROTEIN HERE TO EJECT\n05 / SOLUTE ADJUSTERS\nDRAG TOKENS\nN\nSodium ion\nOUT 10\u201312 \u00b7 IN 7\u20139\nDRAG +1\nDRAG \u22121\nK\nPotassium ion\nOUT 9\u201311 \u00b7 IN 9\u201311\nDRAG +1\nDRAG \u22121\n\nAdd or remove one visible particle at a time. Use this only as a calibration control; the transporter transcript still matters.\n\n06 / ATP RESERVOIR\n0 UNITS\nUNFUELED\nDRAG ATP BURST (+4) INTO THE WELL\n07 / CROSSING LEDGER\n7 EVENTS\nPASSIVE\nNa+ leak\n\u00d72\nATP\nNa+ pump\n\u00d74\nATP\nK+ pump\n\u00d74\nPASS \u00b7 GRADIENT HELD\nDo not lock until the bars hold inside their bands for the visible observation window.\nNEW CELL\nLOCK GRADIENT\nMEMBRANE LOCKED \u00b7 PASS"
